   "heading": "EXAMPLE 1",
   "level": 1,
   "page": 478,
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "kind": "paragraph",
     "marker": null,
     "indent": 1,
     "text": "A DN 200 (NPS 8) run (header) in an oil piping system has a DN 100 (NPS 4) branch at right angles (see Figure H301-1). Both pipes are Schedule 40 API 5L Grade A seamless. The design conditions are 2 068 kPa at 200°C. The fillet welds at the crotch are minimum size in accordance with para. 328.5.4. A corrosion allowance of 2.5 mm is specified. Is additional reinforcement necessary?"
    }
