  {
   "id": "H304",
   "heading": "EXAMPLE 4",
   "level": 1,
   "page": 481,
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "kind": "paragraph",
     "marker": null,
     "indent": 1,
     "text": "A DN 200 (NPS 8) run (header) in an oil piping system has a DN 100 (NPS 4) branch at right angles (see Figure H301-1). Both pipes are Schedule 40 API 5L Grade A seamless. The design conditions are 2 400 kPa at 205°C. It is assumed that the piping system is to remain in service until all metal thickness, in both branch and run, in excess of that required by eq. (3a) of para. 304.1.2 has corroded away so that area A2 as defined in para. 304.3.3(c)(1) is zero. What reinforcement is required for this connection?"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": null,
   "heading": "Solution",
   "level": 2,
   "page": 481,
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "kind": "paragraph",
     "marker": null,
     "indent": 0,
     "text": "1.0."
    },
    {
     "kind": "equation",
     "text": "t h 2.37 mm",
     "indent": 1
    },
    {
     "kind": "equation",
     "text": "t b = = 1.24 mm (2)(110 000)(1.0)(1.0) + (2)(0.4)(2 400)",
     "indent": 1
    },
    {
     "kind": "equation",
     "text": "d 1 = 114.3 − (2)(1.24) 112 mm =",
     "indent": 6
    },
